L2 Knowledge Base - Issue 2 (Missing Shortcuts)
v 1.0, 07/08/2026, status : Draft

Purpose
Investigate and restore missing desktop shortcuts after document-management rollout.

Trigger
Use when users report missing desktop shortcuts after sign-in.

Required access
- Endpoint administrative access
- Intune app/profile assignment visibility
- Event log access
- Incident and change record access

Procedure (navigation > action > expected)
1. Service desk > Incident > Open ticket > Set In Progress.
Expected: ownership and timestamp captured.
2. Service desk > Work notes > Record affected user, host, missing shortcut names.
Expected: issue scope documented.
3. Endpoint > File Explorer > User and Public desktop paths.
Expected: confirm absent, moved, or hidden shortcuts.
4. Endpoint > Start search > Search missing app names.
Expected: confirm app availability independent of shortcut.
5. Endpoint > Settings > Apps > Installed apps.
Expected: confirm app install state.
6. Endpoint > Registry (read-only) > Shell Folders and User Shell Folders desktop entries.
Expected: confirm desktop path mapping/redirection.
7. Event Viewer > Application log > Last 7 days installer/deployment events.
Expected: rollout and error timing evidence captured.
8. Intune > Apps/Profiles for Floor 6 > Review rollout assignment/detection state.
Expected: identify rollout-linked behavior.
9. If rollout-related, pause or scope-limit impacted assignment to Floor 6 only.
Expected: impact contained.
10. Restore shortcuts via approved deployment method.
Expected: shortcuts restored for user.

Verification
- Shortcuts visible again.
- Apps open correctly from shortcuts.
- Second user/device check confirms consistency.

Rollback
1. Restore pre-change assignment scope.
2. Re-sync tested endpoints.
3. Revert restore package if it introduced regression.
4. Escalate with logs and path evidence if unresolved.
